Developer Recommendation
The Contact page should primarily use a contact form rather than publishing multiple individual OCRA email addresses.
Using enquiry categories allows messages to be routed internally while keeping the public contact process simple. It also means responsibilities can change within OCRA without requiring contact information throughout the website to be rewritten.
The general info@ocra.ie address should still be displayed as an alternative contact method.
Social media icons and links should be displayed beneath the contact form.
Only active and verified OCRA social media accounts should be shown. The current Twitter/X link should not be carried across unless a valid OCRA account is confirmed.
Where possible, the form should include basic spam protection and should send the user a clear confirmation after successful submission.

